>>>malloy
source: reviews is duckdb.table('reviews.csv') extend {
  measure: review_count is count()
  measure: avg_rating is avg(Rating)
}

>>>markdown
# What Makes Women Happy With Their Clothes?
I started with a simple question: do all fashion categories satisfy customers equally? I assumed yes. I was wrong.

>>>malloy
run: reviews -> {
  group_by: `Department Name`
  aggregate: review_count, avg_rating
  order_by: avg_rating desc
}

>>>markdown
## The Trend Problem
Trend items have the lowest rating of any department. But ratings alone don't tell the full story — I wanted to know whether customers were actually recommending these items to others.

>>>malloy
run: reviews -> {
  group_by: `Department Name`
  aggregate: recommended is avg(`Recommended IND`) * 100
  order_by: recommended desc
}

>>>markdown
## Does Age Change Anything?
I wondered if younger shoppers were harder to please. Turns out age barely matters — satisfaction is about the category, not the customer.

>>>malloy
run: reviews -> {
  group_by: Age
  aggregate: review_count, avg_rating
  order_by: Age asc
}

>>>markdown
## What This Means
Trend pieces disappoint. Staples deliver. For any retailer, this is a signal worth acting on.